    "description": "Food tourism routes connect ingredients, preparation, markets and meals within a particular landscape or urban setting. Rasht’s documented gastronomy heritage and Tabriz’s historic commercial fabric illustrate complementary ways to interpret food through place, without assuming that a cultural designation establishes an operating tour.",
    "tags": ["Food tourism", "Culinary heritage", "Rasht", "Tabriz", "Markets", "Regional travel"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "ready_for_review",
