    "description": "Iran’s travel infrastructure includes accommodation, transport, booking channels and the people who organize and interpret journeys. Historic caravanserais and adapted buildings in Yazd show the connection between hospitality and heritage, while payment access and changing operating conditions affect whether services are usable by international visitors.",
    "tags": ["Travel infrastructure", "Accommodation", "Transport", "Booking", "Heritage conservation", "Visitor services"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "needs_research",
